nswer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "93710f5b-4706-57af-a1db-085da41d893c" :question/math-academy-id "q-35982" :question/problem "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $P(0,-2,-4)$ and $Q(5,0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $P$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=p+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $P(0,-2,-4)$ and $Q(5,0,1)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =⟨5,0,1⟩-⟨0,-2,-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,2,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311187 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6dee200-f517-5645-87ec-ccf36012e55e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Equation of the Line Passing Through Two Given Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03bb1d80-0e09-5279-ba61-e3b34b1934f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311189} {:answer/id #uuid "3a3de85a-798b-573f-aad2-4cd3b7bca002" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311190} {:answer/id #uuid "b030f7d5-dd54-5e2a-ad3e-f51a1bf0dabc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311191} {:answer/id #uuid "1ce76003-0b7a-50b2-b3a2-fd15f4845c69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311192} {:answer/id #uuid "1ba33e16-89dd-5424-9ffc-a5c450f1db01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b030f7d5-dd54-5e2a-ad3e-f51a1bf0dabc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311191} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ff96cd7-3685-5fde-ab5c-d93df5715d3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311188}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1b5b7d76-7995-5fd2-be2e-9a59c7b1bd88" :question/math-academy-id "q-69772" :question/problem "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $K(-4,-3,-1)$ and $L(1,2,4).$" :question/worked-solution "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $K$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=k+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $k$ is the position vector of $K.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $K(-4,-3,-1)$ and $L(1,2,4),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{KL} \\\\  & =⟨1,2,4⟩-⟨-4,-3,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,5,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311194 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6dee200-f517-5645-87ec-ccf36012e55e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Equation of the Line Passing Through Two Given Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5f765c0-eeaf-5f2c-b9e4-31697a68a5d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311196} {:answer/id #uuid "ae159daa-ae2f-5993-a9fe-a1e4607459af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311197} {:answer/id #uuid "1c19e1e1-2e21-5fc2-9edc-8b90e176e4c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311198} {:answer/id #uuid "fe2fce85-434d-5388-98cb-703efa7f3143" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311199} {:answer/id #uuid "34b93c29-3acc-5628-a96b-2248f84768dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34b93c29-3acc-5628-a96b-2248f84768dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311200} :answer-field/id #uuid "862a8add-701c-5f6a-a20d-4c2c94c89c53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311195}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "51cde5d3-a898-58ba-977d-965c7a803752" :question/math-academy-id "q-77434" :question/problem "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $P(-1,5,4)$ and $Q(3,-1,2).$" :question/worked-solution "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $P$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=p+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $P(-1,5,4)$ and $Q(3,-1,2)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =⟨3,-1,2⟩-⟨-1,5,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,-6,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311201 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6dee200-f517-5645-87ec-ccf36012e55e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Equation of the Line Passing Through Two Given Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f351e16a-0e06-57e7-a17a-c573975b99a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311203} {:answer/id #uuid "cd146d9f-be3e-5bef-8e02-3145fa861502" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311204} {:answer/id #uuid "ffc138a5-17c2-511e-bb6b-fc8c8cf7aa1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311205} {:answer/id #uuid "f292a410-5a51-5aed-83f7-8c8d7efec009" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311206} {:answer/id #uuid "a9829abb-ffba-59da-9845-aa501dc31f18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f351e16a-0e06-57e7-a17a-c573975b99a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311203} :answer-field/id #uuid "589b13ef-662c-5fbf-9694-b33fc4d67853" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311202}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8e23f630-f4c4-5539-9c2d-179afdf462ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-77435" :question/problem "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $M(0,1,0)$ and $N(3,4,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $M$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=m+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $m$ is the position vector of $M.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $M(0,1,0)$ and $N(3,4,-1)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{MN} \\\\  & =⟨3,4,-1⟩-⟨0,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,3,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311208 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c338d1eb-7e13-5089-8dd3-d5ca6eefd4ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points on a Line That Are a Fixed Distance From Another Point on the Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f299e4ee-0d87-5b20-b9c2-616a468cd553" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(6,-6,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(10,18,8)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311210} {:answer/id #uuid "9b81aa93-84f4-569d-9611-f982ef89af8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(10,2,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(2,6,-4)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311211} {:answer/id #uuid "fc89ac3c-5852-5b09-80a0-e4ce2ddea766" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(8,-12,5)$ and ${A}_{2}(7,6,-3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311212} {:answer/id #uuid "a147f309-f3f8-50d0-bd0a-e3cf9539e610" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(6,-6,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(2,6,-4)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311213} {:answer/id #uuid "bf60c65e-1a30-55f7-9f35-bf29135bc1bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(10,2,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(7,6,-3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a147f309-f3f8-50d0-bd0a-e3cf9539e610" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(6,-6,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(2,6,-4)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311213} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ee7d575-a0c4-5892-a256-694602bc0503" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f8ced46a-f7bf-550c-ae94-d64f15be9c59" :question/math-academy-id "q-77442" :question/problem "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(4,0,-1)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨2,-6,3⟩.$ Find all the possible points $A$ on that line such that $PA=7.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨4,0,-1⟩+t⟨2,-6,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $A$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OA} & =⟨4,0,-1⟩+t⟨2,-6,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PA} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨4,0,-1⟩+t⟨2,-6,3⟩)-⟨4,0,-1⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨2,-6,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,-6t,\\,3t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PA=7,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PA & =7 \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PA}| & =7 \\\\ |⟨2t,\\,-6t,\\,3t⟩| & =7 \\\\ \\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+(-6t)^{2}+(3t)^{2}} & =7 \\\\ \\sqrt{49{t}^{2}} & =7 \\\\ \\pm 7t & =7 \\\\ t & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 1$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{1}}=⟨4,0,-1⟩+⟨2,-6,3⟩=⟨6,-6,2⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{2}}=⟨4,0,-1⟩-⟨2,-6,3⟩=⟨2,6,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${A}_{1}(6,-6,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(2,6,-4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311215 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c338d1eb-7e13-5089-8dd3-d5ca6eefd4ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points on a Line That Are a Fixed Distance From Another Point on the Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00372776-9900-5873-b2d8-8af723760951" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${Q}_{1}(6,2,2)$ and ${Q}_{2}(1,0,-2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311217} {:answer/id #uuid "e54b1804-49df-5963-bd11-66814707531f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${Q}_{1}(4,2,6)$ and ${Q}_{2}(1,0,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311218} {:answer/id #uuid "2aaa7882-74d1-5f0e-a190-932cda76b670" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${Q}_{1}(2,0,6)$ and ${Q}_{2}(0,2,-4)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311219} {:answer/id #uuid "f00c74ee-9fcf-54b1-97e8-a6bac73a5b5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${Q}_{1}(2,0,6)$ and ${Q}_{2}(-1,3,-9)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311220} {:answer/id #uuid "0cc8c193-62df-53c3-8f7c-bc7b22d80f1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${Q}_{1}(3,-1,11)$ and ${Q}_{2}(0,2,-4)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2aaa7882-74d1-5f0e-a190-932cda76b670" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${Q}_{1}(2,0,6)$ and ${Q}_{2}(0,2,-4)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311219} :answer-field/id #uuid "13bc0196-3911-5c03-a822-6873c92903a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311216}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ca1265ac-23c6-5e5b-be9c-b56a47160343" :question/math-academy-id "q-77443" :question/problem "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(1,1,1)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨1,-1,5⟩.$ Find all the possible points $Q$ on that line such that $PQ=3\\sqrt{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-1,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $Q$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OQ} & =⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-1,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-1,5⟩)-⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨1,-1,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t,\\,-t,\\,5t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PQ=3\\sqrt{3},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PQ & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ |⟨t,\\,-t,\\,5t⟩| & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{{t}^{2}+(-t)^{2}+(5t)^{2}} & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{27{t}^{2}} & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\pm 3\\sqrt{3}t & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ t & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 1$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{Q}_{1}}=⟨1,1,1⟩+⟨1,-1,5⟩=⟨2,0,6⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{Q}_{2}}=⟨1,1,1⟩-⟨1,-1,5⟩=⟨0,2,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${Q}_{1}(2,0,6)$ and ${Q}_{2}(0,2,-4).$"}]}
